## Routing

| You are asked to | Go to |
|---|---|
| build the next ticket, or any ticket | `.icm/intake/CONTEXT.md` (the loop), then the stub |
| open, fill or finish a pull request | `.github/pull_request_template.md`. The gates sit at its top |
| plan new work | `.icm/intake/CONTEXT.md` (an epic with a breakdown), never a loose list |
| understand the build, its stack and its data | `README.md` |
{%- if release %}
| change what CI checks or how a release is cut | `legible-consulting/.github` (`check-client.yml`, `release.yml`). `ci.yml` here only calls them |
{%- else %}
| change what CI checks | `legible-consulting/.github` (`check-client.yml`). `ci.yml` here only calls it |
{%- endif %}
| change a file the blueprint renders | the blueprint, then `copier update` here |
{%- if uat %}
| read the UAT batch, record the client's sign-off, promote, reset the UAT database, roll back | `.icm/uat/CONTEXT.md` (the whole UAT contract), then its scripts |
{%- endif %}

## Rules

- Client-facing text in `{{ language }}`. Code, commits and notes in English.
- Technical text (stubs, pull request bodies, commits, questions) in Simplified Technical
  English: short active sentences, one instruction each, no semicolons. A question for Jamie
  is numbered and carries a default answer.
- CI is truth: never run build, lint, typecheck, test, format or dev locally. Push, then read
  the `ci` run and the preview{% if monorepo %}s{% endif %}.
- Secrets never in git: names only, values in GitHub or Vercel settings. Flag any plaintext
  credential found.
- One ticket is one branch and one pull request. The pull request moves the stub to `_done/`.
- `main` changes by pull request. Gates are human checkboxes: read them, never tick them. The
  merge is Jamie's.{% if release %} The release is Jamie's merge of the release-please pull
  request.{% elif not uat %} Production follows `main`: the merge is the release.{% endif %}
{%- if uat %}
- A ticket's merge reaches the UAT environment, where the client tests the batch. Production
  moves when Jamie publishes the promotion Release that `promote.sh approve` drafted on the
  client's word. A session never publishes it (`.icm/uat/CONTEXT.md`).
{%- endif %}
